          "title": "A sum of geometric series",
          "graded": true,
          "points": 10,
          "statement": "<p>Prove that the series</p>\n\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}(2^n+1)}{3^n}\\]\n<p>converges absolutely, and compute its sum.</p>",
          "solution": "<p>For every \\(n\\),</p>\n\\[\\left|\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}(2^n+1)}{3^n}\\right|=\\left(\\frac23\\right)^n+\\left(\\frac13\\right)^n.\\]\n<p>Both geometric series converge; their sums are \\(2\\) and \\(1/2\\). Thus the sum of the absolute values is \\(5/2\\), proving absolute convergence. The original terms are \\(-(-2/3)^n-(-1/3)^n\\), so the geometric-series formula and linearity give</p>\n\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}(2^n+1)}{3^n}=-\\frac{-2/3}{1+2/3}-\\frac{-1/3}{1+1/3}=\\frac25+\\frac14=\\frac{13}{20}.\\]",
